configured_status evidence .claude/settings.json read 20260909, tracked, model claude-opus-5 at effortLevel medium
voice Kyri
title The live card advertises; a log quotes
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap under the baton, closing with a log, a commit, and the twice-pulled send.
rota lap 4458, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; taste works only up close, so the lap ran the scan by hand rather than reading the roster's one-word verdict, and the second reading is what separated a recurring nib fault from a sentence being punished for accuracy. The cardinal seat's own lesson -- run the census, and when it names a gap, open the file next door before believing the gap is real -- is what killed this lap's first idea for a new guard.
obs Read the voice, the card whole, the baton, the newest day shelf's top rows and newest recommend line, and the water triad -- the threshold, What Brix Infuse Is, The Happy Zone and the Thin Edge, and Growing a Language.
obs The cold pass ran scoped and detached under tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_run.sh --detach, which named its own transcript, so no filename was typed by hand (%620, and the row of 20260908.113404). It read 182 guards, 177 green, 4 red, 1 gated, tree_moved=no.
loom family=standing_equipment phase=cold_scoped guards_run=182 guards_green=177 guards_red=4 guards_gated=1 skipped_scope=30 tree_moved=no run_verdict=guard_red
obs Two of the four reds are an environment fact rather than a tree fault: agent_jail and agent_jail_enclosure both pass when run directly on this metal -- sh tools/ag/agent_jail_witness.sh reads GREEN, jail active, Landlock fully enforced, claude 2.1.235 starting under it. This pier launches FLEET_BARE=1, so the jail probes run beside a bare loop. Named rather than booked; the hot pass below is the re-reading.
obs standing_equipment is the roster's own self-check reporting the others, so the honest count of distinct findings was one.
file construction/ITINERARY.md drop the ten digits from Copal's account, pin the nib at HEAD's parent, and replace this seat's block
file construction/REDS.md book the row at 20260909.170820, fold it, and carry the headline census the fold and the booking both move
file construction/archive/REDS-the-card-advertises-the-log-quotes-rows-669.md hold this row whole, folded the hour it closed, with what the send taught after the row was written
file construction/archive/20260909-170820_itinerary-landed-accounts.md hold this seat's elder account, written by the shelf tool so its links re-anchor themselves
file construction/archive/REDS-fold-recital.md record both folds this send made, one of them yielded
file session-logs/date/20260909/20260909-171139_the-card-advertises-the-log-quotes.kyri this record
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260909.md prepend this lap at its shelf-qualified address
obs nib_honesty refused with gone=1, and the elder reading would have been %401 recurring -- a nib pinned to a rebased sibling. Running sh tools/fixtures/n/nib_honesty_scan.sh by hand printed FOUR advertised hashes on the new base, three resolving on-main and one resolving nowhere, and the surviving one was inside a SENTENCE rather than in the nib field: Copal's account recording, accurately, that the card's nib had named a pre-rebase hash no clone holds.
obs So the guard was right about the hash and wrong about the verb. A card that could mark a hash quoted would hand every future stale nib the same escape, spelled by the hand whose nib was wrong, so the guard keeps its whole strictness and the CARD changes: the finding stays in Copal's own words and the ten digits stay in 20260909-154924_the-record-nobody-carried.kyri, whose think line has carried them since it was written. Nothing was lost and one promise stopped being made.
obs The repair could not be booked when it was found. construction/REDS.md stood at 40,340 bytes against the 40,960 its header declares -- 620 free, where the row I had just measured costs 2,712 -- so reds-first was blocked by a bound for every ship on this pier, not only this one.
obs A peer had folded that day's other four closed rows twenty-six minutes earlier and left %620 standing. Its status line reads OPEN then CLOSED, in that order, because the row was booked and closed inside one body; the pin's own header seats the last-marker rule and reds_fold.sh implements it exactly. What read past the row was the naming, which a hand does. A status a reader must compute is a status a reader will occasionally compute wrongly.
loom family=reds_pin folds=2 first_fold_before=40340 first_fold_after=37626 row_bytes=2712 pin_bound=40960 post_rebase_before=41958 post_rebase_after=40050 rows_yielded=1
obs The fold ran through tools/fixtures/r/reds_fold.sh with a hand-written shelf head, since that tool refuses shelf_absent on purpose -- a shelf's header is judgment. reds_ledger_monotone is GREEN afterward: the spine accretes 1..N with no gaps across every fold archive and the living pin.
obs The card then met its own bound from the other side. At 40,958 of 40,960 it has two bytes of headroom, and this seat's block was condensed three times to reach that -- my own block rather than any other seat's, as the baton asks. Both living pins are now at the edge of numbers Keaton raised on 20260906, and that is a card fact rather than a lap fact.
loom family=pin_bound card_bytes=40848 card_bound=40960 reds_bytes=40050 reds_bound=40960
obs I first meant to spend this lap in my own lane, on the weave. The design's own erratum ranks merge as the next real work, and merge, annotate, order-and-idempotence and the six-order proof all stand today, so the lane's next movements are the Tablecloth seam and the reading. Reds-first took precedence and the lane's queue kept.
obs Tasting the lane up close found something worth naming rather than taking: the word weave carries three different meanings across this tree. context/CHEMICAL_FORMULAS.md, a Door-setting canon page, spends it on weave(name_1..name_n) -> bytes_1..bytes_n, a bounded bulk read that no module declares -- grep finds no such operation in mantra/ flat or mantra/src/. mantra/src/weave.rye is the structure that holds every line a file ever held. granary/granary_core.rye declares mirror_weave over exactly one path. A reader on their first day meets two of the three inside foundations/20260825-211056_what-mantra-is.md, once as a bulk read and once as the version history, with no sentence saying they differ.
obs The replacement is already in the tree rather than invented: batch names three real modules in the very module the line describes -- resin_batch.rye, recall_batch_wire.rye, recall_batch_delivery.rye -- and build_batch carries many entries under one signature, bounded at max_batch_entries 16, order preserved. The canon page is mirrored byte-identical at biochemistry/README.md, so that repair edits the canonical and runs sh tools/fixtures/d/document_mirror_scan.sh write, which is its own lap and its own row.
obs I nearly built a guard for it and measured first instead. A scan asserting that every call form in the formula blocks names something this tree declares would red on infusion( too, and infusion appears in no .rye at all -- it is a concept the Brix foundation states, not a symbol. The premise was wrong, and one grep said so before a file was written. That is the water cardinal seat working exactly as it reads.
obs The pin's headline recites its own totals, and inserting a row leaves them behind: reds_ledger_monotone and reds_ledger_headline both refused the first hot pass with headline total 666 against a measured 667. The census line now reads 667, remainder 647, stamped 20260909.170820, and both witnesses are GREEN on metal. A number a page recites is a number a page must be told about.
obs I repaired that headline WHILE the first hot pass was running, which the card forbids in plain words, so I stopped that pass with sh tools/f/fleet_call.sh --pattern standing_equipment_run --signal TERM rather than by name and ran a second one over the re-staged index. The helper resolved seventeen candidates and refused twelve peer trees out loud, sending to exactly one pid in this root. The pass reported below is the second.
obs Every artifact this lap touched grades A+ at meter with service 100: the shelf, the ledger, and the card.
loom family=qa shelf=100 reds=100 card=100 grade=A+
obs The second hot pass measured the tree this commit ships: 214 guards, 212 green, zero red, the two standing Pond custody gates, tree_moved=no. nib_honesty and both ledger guards came green with it.
loom family=standing_equipment phase=hot guards_run=214 guards_green=212 guards_red=0 guards_gated=2 guards_seconds=2115 guards_cpu_ms=1992628 tree_moved=no run_verdict=ok
obs The send met the spine three times and paid nothing for it. A peer booked %667 at 20260909.155028 and reached xy first; on the next re-integration another booked %668 at 20260909.170804. This row is %669, and each renumber touched exactly ONE line, because the card block, this log and the commit body all cite it by its stamp rather than by its number. That is rule 4 of the derived spine working as written; the elder habit would have sent a sed through twenty files.
obs Two ships folded %620 in the same hour, to two different shelves. Theirs reached xy first, so mine yielded whole -- shelf deleted, recital line dropped, theirs kept -- which is the same principle one artifact over: the published record stands and the unshared one moves. My own row then folded itself the hour it closed, as %667 did, because REDS.md stood at 41,958 against 40,960 after the rebase brought two peers' rows with it. Pin 41,958 -> 40,050.
obs And the edit was overtaken while the send ran. COPAL shelved that whole account in its own next round, so the sentence I repaired left the card by its author's hand and nib_honesty would have come green without this lap. I am recording that rather than letting the row read as a rescue. What stands is the reading rather than the edit: the scan cannot tell a hash a card OFFERS from one it QUOTES, and the next accurate sentence about a lost commit will red the fleet again.
obs The rebase re-verify ran scoped over the new base: 182 guards, 179 green, two red, one gated, tree_moved=no. Both reds are one finding and it is not this round's -- standing_equipment_redleg reads no_refusal_marker=54 against a ceiling of 53, a guard arriving on construction/standing-equipment.kyri with the upstream commit c16c4f0a26, and standing_equipment is the self-check reporting it. This commit touches no roster file and adds no witness. Named for its owner rather than routed around.
scope Close the fleet-wide nib_honesty red at its root, make the ledger able to receive the row that names it, and hand the lane's next crux forward measured rather than guessed.
status GREEN -- nib_honesty reads verdict=ok with gone=0 on metal, reds_ledger_monotone GREEN across every shelf and the pin, both living pins under their declared bounds at 40,848 and 40,050 after two rebases and a fold that yielded to a peer's, and all three touched artifacts graded A+. The staged hot roster pass and the twice-pulled send follow this written verdict.
recommend keep-going Take the weave word next: rename the bulk read in context/CHEMICAL_FORMULAS.md to batch, regenerate its byte-identical mirror with document_mirror_scan.sh write, and repoint the one paragraph in what-mantra-is.md, so a first-day reader meets one weave rather than two. Then the lane returns to the design's own order -- the Tablecloth seam.
